WEBVTT

00:02.961 --> 00:05.038
We are preparing your tea
at the moment.

00:05.038 --> 00:06.924
Thank you very much.

00:10.844 --> 00:13.138
Oh my, did you see fairies?

00:15.807 --> 00:17.768
They live in my house.

00:17.768 --> 00:19.228
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:24.523 --> 00:30.021
♪Leisurely, leisurely,
let's slowly familiarize ourselves♪

00:30.021 --> 00:35.072
(A Journey Through Another World:
Raising Kids While Adventuring)

00:36.161 --> 00:41.025
♪The adventure to a new world is beginning♪

00:41.025 --> 00:45.712
♪Into a journey where
we can find fun things♪

00:47.589 --> 00:52.097
♪There are many encounters,
it's so exciting♪

00:52.097 --> 00:59.142
♪If you're with your family,
the things you can do will multiply♪

00:59.142 --> 01:02.062
♪It's okay to worry,
but you must not be overprotective♪

01:02.062 --> 01:05.023
♪I want you to praise me when
I try something and succeed♪

01:05.023 --> 01:07.818
♪It will be a wonderful party
if we can do this and that♪

01:07.818 --> 01:12.531
♪Because we will be together forever♪

01:12.099 --> 01:16.493
♪Please pat my head♪

01:16.493 --> 01:18.996
♪With your hand that I truly love♪

01:18.996 --> 01:24.668
♪I will send you thank you from
the deepest part of my heart, okay?♪

01:24.668 --> 01:27.627
♪Please pat me more♪

01:27.629 --> 01:30.757
♪See me with those eyes
filled with kindness♪

01:30.757 --> 01:37.097
♪I want this smile to last,
forever and ever♪

01:37.097 --> 01:42.561
♪Leisurely, leisurely,
let's slowly walk on♪

01:43.061 --> 01:48.442
♪Leisurely, Yururing,
I am happy, Travel Days♪

01:51.079 --> 01:54.489
(Can We... Have Friends...?)

01:54.489 --> 01:55.084
(Can We... Have Friends...?)
After a brief introduction,

01:55.084 --> 01:56.575
After a brief introduction,

01:56.575 --> 02:00.412
we explained in detail
how I found the Ripple Labyrinth,

02:00.412 --> 02:05.292
and relayed the information gathered
by the investigation team to Cedric.

02:06.046 --> 02:10.213
It's hard to believe a labyrinth
is found in my territory.

02:10.213 --> 02:12.174
I must thank you, Takumi.

02:12.174 --> 02:15.052
Yes. Now more people
will come to our city.

02:15.552 --> 02:18.722
In this world,
the labyrinth is a source of money.

02:18.722 --> 02:21.767
If the news about
the new labyrinth spreads,

02:21.767 --> 02:23.894
many adventurers
will come to challenge,

02:23.894 --> 02:26.229
so the inns
and restaurants will flourish.

02:26.229 --> 02:29.191
Items from the labyrinth
will be sold in the guild,

02:29.191 --> 02:32.277
and once sold to merchants,
the guild will also flourish.

02:33.612 --> 02:37.658
The economy in various sectors will move
and the tax revenue will also increase,

02:37.658 --> 02:40.327
and as a result,
the territory's economy will prosper.

02:41.536 --> 02:44.498
I thought it'd end up badly,

02:44.498 --> 02:50.338
but I'm glad I can repay some of the care
the Risner family has given us.

02:51.922 --> 02:56.157
This will be the fifth labyrinth
found in the Kingdom of Gaudia.

02:56.614 --> 02:58.284
Here is the list.

02:59.346 --> 03:00.667
I see.

03:01.188 --> 03:05.234
Half of the labyrinth in my obtained
knowledge is still undiscovered.

03:05.758 --> 03:08.594
Surprisingly, those close to the city
also haven't been found.

03:09.314 --> 03:14.319
I must be careful when tackling labyrinths
so this won't happen again.

03:14.319 --> 03:18.448
If you are interested in other labyrinths,
you can take the map.

03:18.448 --> 03:19.825
Thank you very much.

03:21.743 --> 03:23.245
A notification sound?

03:23.245 --> 03:25.288
Is the map being updated?

03:25.288 --> 03:27.457
I'll check that later.

03:28.738 --> 03:30.074
Syl sure works fast...

03:31.128 --> 03:33.213
Wait, is he watching constantly?

03:33.755 --> 03:34.715
Oh, crap!

03:35.382 --> 03:37.509
Mr. Takumi, is anything wrong?

03:37.509 --> 03:38.978
Ah, nothing.

03:40.804 --> 03:45.142
By the way, how far did the scout team
go into the labyrinth?

03:45.142 --> 03:48.103
They seem to only skim
the first floor.

03:48.105 --> 03:50.858
They are having difficulty
with the entrance.

03:51.898 --> 03:57.362
My wording may be crude,
but there is no victim, right?

03:57.362 --> 03:58.572
They are fine.

03:59.573 --> 04:03.881
The scout members have stamina
and we picked the best swimmers.

04:04.369 --> 04:07.205
We also gave them magical items.

04:07.205 --> 04:08.029
Magical items?

04:08.029 --> 04:10.094
Is it something
to aid breathing?

04:10.941 --> 04:11.752
Correct.

04:11.752 --> 04:16.298
It's not that efficient,
but they have the Wind Stone.

04:16.298 --> 04:18.967
That device steadily conjures air.

04:19.801 --> 04:21.261
So they have those!

04:24.043 --> 04:25.988
That calms me down.

04:26.079 --> 04:29.041
Next is about the medal of honor.

04:29.603 --> 04:34.775
You may have known it already,
but there's a medal from the kingdom.

04:34.775 --> 04:37.319
Uh, I don't need a medal...

04:37.319 --> 04:41.156
More importantly, will the name
of the discoverer be announced?

04:41.156 --> 04:43.185
We report it to the kingdom,

04:43.187 --> 04:45.648
but they don't always
officially announce it.

04:46.316 --> 04:49.122
Some remain unannounced in the past.

04:49.586 --> 04:53.124
Do you dislike being known
by the public?

04:53.126 --> 04:56.588
If you're named as the discoverer,
you'll be showered with praises.

04:56.588 --> 05:00.425
I don't want to stand out,
so I'd rather not

05:00.425 --> 05:01.051
I understand.

05:01.051 --> 05:04.221
I'll make sure His Majesty is informed.

05:04.221 --> 05:05.472
Thank you.

05:05.472 --> 05:09.184
But make sure to take the medal, okay?

05:09.184 --> 05:11.144
O-Okay.

05:11.812 --> 05:14.523
That's all about the labyrinth.

05:14.523 --> 05:15.899
Thanks for your work.

05:15.899 --> 05:18.536
Please allow me to excuse myself.

05:19.861 --> 05:24.908
By the way, a problem happened
at the guild yesterday, right?

05:25.007 --> 05:27.661
I am very sorry!

05:27.661 --> 05:31.081
For staff with a duty of confidentiality
to shout the content of a card,

05:31.081 --> 05:32.999
it is highly unacceptable!

05:32.999 --> 05:36.503
We are deeply sorry to Mr. Takumi.

05:37.224 --> 05:40.841
So the incident at the guild
was relayed to Mr. Cedric, too?

05:40.841 --> 05:44.094
We'll enforce information control
better next time.

05:44.636 --> 05:46.054
Please forgive us.

05:46.054 --> 05:51.017
Uh, the guild master and the staff
have apologized to me, so it's fine.

05:51.081 --> 05:56.189
Mr. Cedric has excellent
data-gathering staff.

05:56.773 --> 06:00.036
If Mr. Takumi said so,
we won't punish you further.

06:00.036 --> 06:04.239
But please make sure
that will never happen again.

06:04.239 --> 06:05.615
Y-Yes, Sir!

06:05.615 --> 06:07.033
Please excuse me!

06:09.452 --> 06:13.707
I have received the report
of your arrival in the city,

06:13.707 --> 06:17.252
but I didn't expect
the guild to trouble you.

06:17.061 --> 06:19.004
- I am very sorry.
- Please!  - Excuse me!

06:17.252 --> 06:19.337
- I am very sorry.

06:19.337 --> 06:21.019
- A report of arrival?
- Please!  - Excuse me!

06:21.214 --> 06:25.635
I heard that you'll be coming
from Issac's letter,

06:25.635 --> 06:30.098
so I told the guard to report
if you arrived.

06:30.098 --> 06:34.728
I was worried because
it took a while until you came here.

06:35.604 --> 06:38.899
I-I am sorry, we were late to meet you.

06:38.899 --> 06:42.235
It's all right. I believe you have
looked around the city, right?

06:42.235 --> 06:44.029
Yes, just for a bit.

06:44.029 --> 06:46.531
- The sea!
- So fun!

06:47.699 --> 06:50.493
Please, enjoy your time in the city.

06:50.493 --> 06:51.661
- Okay!
- Okay!

06:51.661 --> 06:52.913
Thank you very much.

06:54.456 --> 06:58.416
Lord Cedric, the lunch is ready.

06:58.418 --> 07:00.879
Then we will soon excuse...

07:00.879 --> 07:02.464
Now, Mr. Takumi!

07:03.006 --> 07:04.925
Let's head to the dining room!

07:05.592 --> 07:06.885
Eh?

07:09.346 --> 07:11.806
This gives such a noble vibe!

07:13.642 --> 07:15.644
Let me introduce you, Mr. Takumi.

07:15.644 --> 07:17.771
This is my wife, Olivie.

07:17.771 --> 07:19.856
Welcome to our abode.

07:19.856 --> 07:22.817
Thank you for having us.
I am Takumi.

07:22.817 --> 07:24.631
And here are my sons.

07:24.986 --> 07:26.905
Good day, I am Theodore.

07:26.905 --> 07:28.281
I'm Latis!

07:30.064 --> 07:31.069
Did you find fairies?

07:32.869 --> 07:34.079
- Fairies...
- Fairies...

07:34.079 --> 07:38.625
We also have a daughter, but she is
too young so we can't have her here.

07:39.167 --> 07:42.545
Hello. They are Alan and Elena.

07:42.545 --> 07:45.215
Come on, say hi to them.

07:45.215 --> 07:47.083
I'm Alan.

07:47.084 --> 07:48.398
I'm Elena.

07:51.429 --> 07:53.932
Are they being shy?

07:53.932 --> 07:55.892
Or anxious?

07:55.892 --> 07:59.896
They have never met anyone
of their own age, after all.

08:00.814 --> 08:03.775
Sorry for this, Theodore, Latis.

08:03.775 --> 08:07.814
These kids are quite shy to strangers,

08:07.815 --> 08:10.115
please be kind to them.

08:10.115 --> 08:11.282
- Okay!
- Okay!

08:18.081 --> 08:19.874
It's delicious!

08:19.874 --> 08:24.212
It only has salt as seasoning,
but it's light and easy to eat!

08:28.049 --> 08:29.639
It's delicious, right?

08:29.064 --> 08:30.552
Yeah!

08:30.552 --> 08:32.554
Oh, right, Mr. Takumi.

08:32.554 --> 08:35.015
Isaac wrote in the letter saying that

08:35.015 --> 08:38.476
you introduced new popular
breads in Shireen.

08:38.476 --> 08:40.979
Mr. Issac wrote that much?!

08:40.979 --> 08:48.486
Yes. Actually breads that don't need
detailed recipes have also spread here.

08:49.195 --> 08:52.866
Issac told me there are also
cream bread and red bean buns.

08:52.866 --> 08:56.077
He boasted about
how delicious they are.

08:56.077 --> 08:57.162
Eh?!

08:57.162 --> 08:59.622
So he likes it that much...

08:59.622 --> 09:02.792
Would you please tell us
those recipes as well?

09:03.046 --> 09:05.503
Of course, we'll reward you.

09:05.503 --> 09:07.714
No, I don't need a reward.

09:08.256 --> 09:11.676
Cream bread is Alan and Elena's favorite,

09:11.676 --> 09:15.055
and I'll be happy
if Bailey will have it too.

09:15.055 --> 09:16.181
- Cream!
- Cream!

09:16.181 --> 09:18.099
I want to taste it!

09:20.081 --> 09:24.397
I don't have enough
for everyone to eat...

09:24.397 --> 09:26.024
- Big Bro.
- Big Bro.

09:26.024 --> 09:27.692
- I want jelly!
- I want jelly!

09:27.692 --> 09:28.985
Now?

09:28.985 --> 09:30.945
What is a jelly?

09:30.945 --> 09:32.822
It's jiggly.

09:32.822 --> 09:34.657
And smooth.

09:36.618 --> 09:40.008
It's a dessert
often eaten after a meal.

09:40.008 --> 09:44.459
If you don't mind,
would you allow us to eat it too?

09:44.459 --> 09:46.669
- Eh?
- Is it too much trouble?

09:46.669 --> 09:48.063
N-No! It's just...

09:48.063 --> 09:52.133
It uses a peculiar ingredient.

09:52.133 --> 09:55.095
It may not suit nobles very much...

09:55.095 --> 09:57.597
So that's what you mean.

09:57.597 --> 10:01.226
Then please let us guess
what ingredient it is.

10:01.226 --> 10:03.978
- I wonder what.
- Maybe something new.

10:04.687 --> 10:07.982
They are surprisingly very curious.

10:07.982 --> 10:11.111
It's obviously not commonly
used as food in Ethelldia,

10:11.111 --> 10:13.738
I hope they won't get mad.

10:18.535 --> 10:22.247
Oh my! It's refreshing and so delicious!

10:22.247 --> 10:24.029
It's so smooth and easy to eat!

10:24.029 --> 10:26.793
- This is so delicious!
- Yeah, so good!

10:26.793 --> 10:27.919
Glad to hear.

10:27.919 --> 10:30.255
- It's yummy, Big Bro!
- It's yummy, Big Bro!

10:31.631 --> 10:35.718
But I can't fathom
what ingredients you used for this.

10:35.718 --> 10:38.138
- Appe fruit?
- Or milk?

10:38.138 --> 10:42.142
Now, now, we can't say Appe
and milk are peculiar, right?

10:42.142 --> 10:43.726
I wonder...

10:44.519 --> 10:48.106
I have no idea.
May I ask what it is?

10:48.106 --> 10:49.774
- Slime!
- Slime!

10:49.774 --> 10:51.025
What?

10:51.734 --> 10:53.017
Jiggly jiggly!

10:53.171 --> 10:54.529
Smooth!

10:54.529 --> 10:57.323
- Did you mean slime, the monster?
- Yes!

10:57.323 --> 10:59.868
Actually, when we arrived in Shireen...

10:59.868 --> 11:01.202
- Big Bro!
- Big Bro!

11:01.202 --> 11:04.664
- We defeated slimes!
- Drop items!

11:04.664 --> 11:06.749
You got so many of them.

11:08.126 --> 11:12.046
(Slime Jelly)
Safe for humans. Melt upon heating.

11:13.381 --> 11:15.508
What should I do with all of this?

11:15.508 --> 11:19.022
It's written as jelly,
so can we eat it as jelly?

11:19.022 --> 11:20.263
- Jelly?
- Jelly?

11:20.263 --> 11:23.391
It has no effect,
so I think it's safe to eat.

11:23.391 --> 11:24.976
Let's try it out.

11:24.976 --> 11:26.477
- Okay!
- Okay!

11:27.002 --> 11:28.938
First, heat the fruit juice in a pot.

11:30.148 --> 11:32.275
And put slime jelly in to melt.

11:34.011 --> 11:36.487
Then pour it into a glass.

11:36.487 --> 11:39.024
And use daily magic
to cool it down instantly.

11:41.117 --> 11:42.535
It's done!

11:42.535 --> 11:44.245
It's jiggly!

11:46.706 --> 11:48.458
Yep, it's yummy!

11:48.458 --> 11:50.168
- So good!
- So good!

11:51.169 --> 11:53.063
So that happened...

11:54.214 --> 11:58.176
This is the slime that is useless
as drug and poison?

11:58.176 --> 12:00.595
I can't believe it can be
made into a dessert.

12:00.595 --> 12:04.057
Has Issac tried this one out?

12:04.057 --> 12:05.516
No, he hasn't.

12:05.516 --> 12:07.227
I see!

12:08.519 --> 12:11.189
Then I'll boast about this back to him!

12:11.189 --> 12:15.528
Eh?! Does he want to counter him
for boasting about cream bread?!

12:15.053 --> 12:17.278
- Mr. Takumi!
- Y-Yes?

12:17.278 --> 12:20.698
Can we buy this recipe from you?

12:20.698 --> 12:22.784
No problem at all.

12:22.784 --> 12:25.203
Let's sell this in shops!

12:25.203 --> 12:27.664
Let's procure slime jelly immediately!

12:27.664 --> 12:32.377
However, My Lord,
it will take time to gather them.

12:32.829 --> 12:38.509
It's the cheapest item, not even
the low-rank adventure will pick them up.

12:40.635 --> 12:43.179
Then why don't we try breeding it?

12:43.179 --> 12:44.305
What?!

12:44.305 --> 12:47.433
Mr. Cedric will begin a slime farm?!

12:48.142 --> 12:50.812
He went all out with the plan...

12:50.812 --> 12:53.382
I can't thank you enough.

12:53.802 --> 12:57.652
Please, do spend your night
at the mansion while you are in Bailey.

12:57.652 --> 13:00.363
I don't want to trouble you further.

13:00.363 --> 13:01.864
I booked a lodging too.

13:01.864 --> 13:03.491
Just cancel it!

13:03.491 --> 13:07.078
We'll contact the lodging
so don't worry about it.

13:08.538 --> 13:10.079
I can't say no to that smile!

13:13.251 --> 13:16.462
Please play with our children as well.

13:16.462 --> 13:21.092
Alan and Elena rarely meet
children in their age,

13:21.092 --> 13:23.428
so I am very glad about it.

13:23.428 --> 13:27.056
Alan, Elena, let's play a lot!

13:32.228 --> 13:34.131
- Let's play a lot.
- Let's play a lot.

13:38.526 --> 13:40.037
The Risner family's bed is so soft,
that we slept so well at night.

13:40.037 --> 13:42.004
- So soft!
The Risner family's bed is so soft,
that we slept so well at night.

13:42.004 --> 13:42.864
The Risner family's bed is so soft,
that we slept so well at night.

13:45.095 --> 13:47.588
Good morning.

13:47.589 --> 13:48.995
You wake up early.

13:48.995 --> 13:50.788
Did you have a great sleep?

13:50.788 --> 13:52.004
We did, indeed.

13:52.004 --> 13:53.958
- It's soft!
- So comfortable!

13:53.958 --> 13:55.418
Glad to hear it.

13:55.418 --> 13:57.337
You're also early, Mr. Cedric

13:57.337 --> 14:01.132
I just received Issac's reply
to my mail yesterday.

14:01.132 --> 14:02.633
Eh? Already?

14:02.633 --> 14:05.392
There's a teleportation device
at the guild.

14:06.304 --> 14:10.433
The device can't send people
like those in the labyrinth,

14:10.433 --> 14:12.977
but we can send things
to faraway places.

14:13.686 --> 14:16.647
- I see, that's practical.
- Yes.

14:17.148 --> 14:20.061
Issac also sent this as urgent.

14:20.061 --> 14:23.279
Urgent?! Is there a problem?

14:23.279 --> 14:26.783
No. He purposely sent it in a rush.

14:27.007 --> 14:30.703
It seems he's frustrated
hearing me bragging.

14:30.703 --> 14:33.664
To put it simply, I teased him.

14:33.664 --> 14:36.834
- Brag? Tease?
- Yes.

14:36.834 --> 14:40.338
I bragged about eating jelly
in my letter yesterday.

14:40.338 --> 14:42.924
But I keep the ingredients in secret.

14:42.924 --> 14:46.135
Eh?! What are these brothers doing?!

14:46.137 --> 14:48.439
Don't tell me they hate each other?!

14:49.663 --> 14:54.442
Issac's competitive side
seems to not change at all.

14:55.561 --> 15:00.271
After being a knight,
he is better at masking his feelings.

15:03.111 --> 15:07.031
Lately, he hasn't been
expressing things honestly,

15:07.031 --> 15:09.492
but this one feels nostalgic.

15:09.492 --> 15:11.016
Could it be...

15:11.016 --> 15:13.621
Mr. Cedric always doted
on his little brother

15:13.621 --> 15:17.505
while playing around
and teasing him since young.

15:18.042 --> 15:20.461
So Mr. Issac who always teases Sir Vault

15:20.461 --> 15:23.464
would be the one teased
if it's against his brother...

15:23.464 --> 15:24.674
I see...

15:25.004 --> 15:26.717
(Creak, Creak, Creak)

15:26.717 --> 15:27.086
(Creak, Creak, Creak)
Hey!

15:27.885 --> 15:29.022
Sorry!

15:29.221 --> 15:30.346
No problem.

15:30.346 --> 15:32.807
(Shireen City)

15:32.807 --> 15:36.687
Huh... It feels like someone
is gossiping about me.

15:37.445 --> 15:38.701
Just my imagination...

15:40.012 --> 15:41.594
This one, though...

15:42.733 --> 15:43.923
Issac!

15:44.485 --> 15:46.446
Hey, Issac!

15:46.446 --> 15:49.332
You look gloomy.

15:49.924 --> 15:51.675
Is that a letter from home?

15:52.016 --> 15:53.661
Anything wrong?

15:53.661 --> 15:57.623
Well, you see...
There are a lot of things...

15:57.623 --> 15:59.333
You don't seem like yourself.

15:59.333 --> 16:02.036
It's rare for you to be silent.

16:02.837 --> 16:05.423
Are you an imposter?!

16:05.423 --> 16:06.549
Captain.

16:06.549 --> 16:09.343
You must be thinking of something rude.

16:09.343 --> 16:11.512
N-No, not at all, really.

16:12.263 --> 16:14.305
So, what's wrong?

16:14.307 --> 16:17.435
Takumi and the others
have arrived at Bailey.

16:17.435 --> 16:20.229
What? Isn't that too fast?

16:20.229 --> 16:21.856
He has kids with him, right?

16:21.856 --> 16:26.652
Well, let's just say
"It's a Takumi thing".

16:27.487 --> 16:31.991
So, your brother reported
Takumi has arrived?

16:31.991 --> 16:35.369
Looks like he has found a new labyrinth.

16:35.369 --> 16:38.122
- What? In Bailey?
- Yes.

16:38.122 --> 16:41.042
That's huge news! Is that true?

16:41.042 --> 16:44.837
That's true.
It's a water-type mid-level labyrinth.

16:44.837 --> 16:46.038
Unbelievable.

16:46.038 --> 16:49.055
Then, why is your face so gloomy?

16:50.092 --> 16:54.263
The person who found
that labyrinth was Takumi.

16:54.263 --> 16:55.473
Wha...

16:55.473 --> 16:57.517
What?!

16:58.434 --> 17:00.269
What the heck is that guy doing?!

17:00.269 --> 17:03.022
You can't just simply stumble
on a labyrinth!

17:03.022 --> 17:06.015
But well, that's something he might do.

17:08.011 --> 17:11.003
Hey, is there anything else?

17:11.003 --> 17:14.617
The finding of a new labyrinth
will be reported to the kingdom.

17:14.617 --> 17:20.498
Well, a direct report to the royal family
will make your brother very busy.

17:20.498 --> 17:24.752
More importantly, the name of
the discoverer will be reported.

17:24.752 --> 17:26.337
They will.

17:28.214 --> 17:31.217
The King will surely call Takumi
to the royal capital.

17:31.217 --> 17:32.076
Totally.

17:32.076 --> 17:37.223
We've reported about the Forest of Gaia
and the slave trader cases, too.

17:37.223 --> 17:41.727
They won't leave him be
since he found a labyrinth on top of that.

17:42.436 --> 17:44.272
Rumors will soon spread.

17:44.939 --> 17:46.983
He already stands out
by bringing kids.

17:47.065 --> 17:51.279
If there are morons with interest
who angered Takumi...

17:51.946 --> 17:55.533
He might leave the country instantly.

17:55.533 --> 17:57.159
I agree...

17:57.702 --> 17:59.287
How to say it...

17:59.287 --> 18:03.874
I don't see him having any
attachment to the country at all.

18:04.792 --> 18:09.063
But for us, if he leaves
we will lose a huge human power.

18:09.063 --> 18:11.132
To prevent that,

18:11.132 --> 18:16.762
let's have our branch leader write
to the knights in the royal capital.

18:16.762 --> 18:20.391
Yeah. I'll contact my home just in case.

18:20.391 --> 18:21.976
And one more thing...

18:22.727 --> 18:25.187
I'm interested in this jelly stuff.

18:25.187 --> 18:27.315
What? What is this about?

18:27.315 --> 18:29.609
Apparently, it's a new dessert.

18:29.609 --> 18:35.364
Takumi seemed to give my brother some
and he said it was so good,

18:35.364 --> 18:39.091
so he got Takumi's permission
to open up a new business.

18:39.091 --> 18:40.828
What?!

18:40.828 --> 18:44.054
He found a labyrinth
and created a new dessert as well?!

18:44.054 --> 18:48.336
He just arrived and
already made a ruckus?!

18:50.657 --> 18:52.325
After the letter incident,

18:52.327 --> 18:55.058
Mr. Cedric invited us
to the morning market.

18:56.051 --> 18:59.847
It would be a commotion if the lord
of the land, Mr. Cedric, was found,

18:59.847 --> 19:01.223
so he disguised himself.

19:01.223 --> 19:06.646
Lately, it appears a unique food
is being sold at the seaside stall.

19:06.646 --> 19:08.898
It's known to be really good.

19:08.898 --> 19:11.317
It's so popular that
the queue is extremely long.

19:11.317 --> 19:13.653
That's intriguing...

19:13.653 --> 19:15.995
Father! It must be over there!

19:15.996 --> 19:16.864
Yes.

19:16.864 --> 19:17.948
Let's hurry!

19:36.258 --> 19:38.219
Alan, Elena, take my hand.

19:47.436 --> 19:49.397
What a crowd.

19:49.397 --> 19:51.315
What is being sold here?

19:51.816 --> 19:53.776
It seems to be grilled clam.

19:54.276 --> 19:56.779
It's a taste like never before...

19:56.779 --> 19:59.099
It's said they use a seasoning
called soy sauce...

19:59.099 --> 20:01.492
Soy sauce...

20:01.492 --> 20:03.044
Mr. Takumi?

20:03.045 --> 20:04.453
Well, nothing...

20:04.453 --> 20:07.206
Oh! It's you guys!

20:07.206 --> 20:11.919
You don't have to queue!
You taught me this, after all!

20:11.919 --> 20:12.837
Huh?

20:12.837 --> 20:14.296
Are they your companions?

20:14.296 --> 20:16.632
Here, just eat away!

20:17.717 --> 20:19.135
Mr. Takumi?

20:19.135 --> 20:20.344
- Scallop!
- Scallop!

20:23.305 --> 20:26.308
I'm surprised that is your doing.

20:26.308 --> 20:27.768
Sorry for that.

20:30.229 --> 20:31.188
It's so good!

20:31.188 --> 20:33.649
- You're right, it's so good!
- Yeah!

20:35.151 --> 20:36.861
Mr. Takumi.

20:36.861 --> 20:40.281
Could you tell me
what this soy sauce thing is?

20:40.281 --> 20:44.577
Soy sauce is the sap of a tree called
Kokuichi that grows in the labyrinth.

20:44.577 --> 20:48.581
Then it is sold in shops
that sell labyrinth items.

20:48.581 --> 20:49.029
Indeed.

20:49.029 --> 20:51.542
Let's visit the shop after this.

20:51.542 --> 20:52.752
- Yay!
- Hurray!

20:53.461 --> 20:54.076
Big Bro!

20:54.761 --> 20:56.213
I want more.

20:56.213 --> 20:57.465
All right, all right.

20:57.465 --> 20:59.842
You two love this taste too, I see.

21:01.927 --> 21:03.971
This is the Fiji Trading Company,

21:03.971 --> 21:06.432
it gathers items found in labyrinths,

21:06.432 --> 21:08.684
and is a prominent shop
in the Kingdom of Guadia.

21:09.393 --> 21:13.355
Mr. Cedric had to speak
with the chief of the company

21:13.355 --> 21:16.901
so while we were waiting,
we looked around the shop.

21:18.011 --> 21:19.612
- Red bean paste!
- Red bean paste!

21:19.612 --> 21:20.905
Alan, Elena.

21:21.697 --> 21:23.491
These are red beans.

21:23.491 --> 21:26.202
You get red bean paste after steaming it.

21:26.202 --> 21:27.661
- Red bean paste?
- Red bean paste?

21:27.661 --> 21:31.582
You have heard of red bean bun
from your father, right?

21:31.582 --> 21:33.083
Oh, I've heard of it!

21:33.083 --> 21:37.254
It's the bread that has been popular
in Shireen lately, right?

21:37.254 --> 21:40.883
Yes. This is the ingredient
for the stuffing.

21:40.883 --> 21:42.718
- What?!
- Is that so?

21:42.718 --> 21:44.168
It's delicious.

21:44.169 --> 21:45.429
So sweet!

21:45.429 --> 21:48.182
I'll let you have a taste next time.

21:48.182 --> 21:49.892
- Yay!
- Thank you very much!

21:49.892 --> 21:52.092
Mr. Takumi, sorry for the wait.

21:52.093 --> 21:52.895
It's okay.

21:53.854 --> 21:56.696
I think I have seen that mark before...

21:57.316 --> 22:03.003
I might seen it at the entrance,
but I think it was in another place...

22:07.451 --> 22:08.911
Oh, I remember!

22:08.911 --> 22:11.163
(Sunken Ship (Dietlinde))

22:11.163 --> 22:14.349
That's the sunken ship I retrieved
at the mermaid village!

22:28.347 --> 22:32.601
♪Forever, all the time♪

22:32.601 --> 22:35.312
♪I just can't keep crying♪

22:35.312 --> 22:36.814
♪Ah! Ah!♪

22:36.814 --> 22:40.442
♪In happy moments and sad moments♪

22:40.442 --> 22:43.007
♪If I am with you♪

22:44.738 --> 22:47.074
♪Such a good weather♪

22:47.074 --> 22:50.661
♪Today, let's go slowly♪

22:50.661 --> 22:53.205
♪While taking detours♪

22:53.205 --> 22:57.751
♪The clear sky,
the wind caressing my cheeks♪

22:57.751 --> 23:01.005
♪And your gentle gaze♪

23:01.005 --> 23:04.258
♪Beyond an unknown road♪

23:04.258 --> 23:06.001
♪The wind blows past♪

23:06.001 --> 23:08.804
♪The curtain of light sways♪

23:09.763 --> 23:13.392
♪Maybe we should try going
I just feel like it♪

23:13.392 --> 23:20.019
♪No matter what happens
we can laugh anyway♪

23:22.401 --> 23:26.405
♪Forever, all the time♪

23:26.405 --> 23:29.158
♪I just can't keep crying♪

23:29.158 --> 23:30.659
♪Ah! Ah!♪

23:30.659 --> 23:34.163
♪In happy moments and sad moments♪

23:34.163 --> 23:37.041
♪If I am with you♪

23:38.208 --> 23:42.713
♪I am sure I'll be content♪

23:45.006 --> 23:45.009
(Next Episode)

23:45.964 --> 23:49.134
- Vector!
- Did a good job!

23:49.134 --> 23:50.008
(Next Episode)
(Vector Did a Good Job!)
